{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.VolumeFromRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.VolumeFromRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.volume_form_is_nondegen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.volume_form_is_nondegen","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L57-L67","doc":"Given a volume form factorisation, condition (iii) of the QOU\n(non-degenerate volume form) is satisfied.\n\nNow a derivation rather than a re-export: the epimorphism follows from\n`epsilon_iso`, where before it *was* the hypothesis `epsilon_epi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.epsilon_iso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.epsilon_iso","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L55-L55","doc":"**Non-degeneracy**: ε is an isomorphism (bean `qou-n1dj`, 2026-08-22).\n\nWas `epsilon_epi : Epi epsilon`, which made `volume_form_is_nondegen`\nbelow a restatement of its own hypothesis.  This block's prose is\nexplicit about what non-degeneracy means here — \"for ε to be\nnon-degenerate, we must have rank(Λ²V) = 1\" — and `rank(Λ²V) = 1` is\n`C(N,2) = 1`, i.e. `N = 2` (`exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff`).  Epi alone\ngives only `C(N,2) ≠ 0`, i.e. `N ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The factorisation: ev ∘ (id ⊗ φ) = ε ∘ π. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.epsilon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.epsilon","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The volume form ε : Λ²V → 𝟙. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.proj","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The projection π : V ⊗ V → Λ²V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.eval","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The evaluation ev : V ⊗ V∨ → 𝟙. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.phi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.phi","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The symplectic isomorphism φ : V → V∨ with φ∨ = -φ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.exteriorSquare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.exteriorSquare","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L36-L36","doc":"The exterior square Λ²V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.V_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.V_dual","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L34-L34","doc":"The dual V∨. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.V","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L32-L32","doc":"The fundamental object V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VolumeFormFactorisation","kind":"structure","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/volume-from-rigidity.lean#L26-L55","doc":"**Volume form factorisation**: for a symplectically self-dual object,\nthe evaluation factors through the exterior square. ","signatureChunk":0}]}